      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 13, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "k", "low": 2, "high": 8, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.9,
      "why": "Only family that can plausibly satisfy both the 50 MSPS throughput and 2^-12 max error constraints. k>=4 reduces cycles/result to <=7, making 50 MSPS reachable at realistic sky130 Fmax. Ranges cover the minimum-power feasible region: W just above quantization limit, N just enough for CORDIC accuracy, small guards, and k spanning the parallelism vs. critical-path trade-off."
    },
    {
      "family": "iterative",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 13, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.1,
      "why": "Small budget to confirm infeasibility. With N~14 for 2^-12 accuracy, iterative needs ~17 cycles/result, requiring Fmax > 850 MHz for 50 MSPS, which is implausible in sky130. If any design unexpectedly meets both constraints, it would be a very low-power Pareto point worth capturing."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The 50 MSPS throughput constraint combined with the 2^-12 max error requirement forces a multi-cycle architecture with enough parallelism. Iterative computes one micro-rotation per cycle, so for N~14 it needs ~17 cycles/result, requiring Fmax > 850 MHz to hit 50 MSPS, which is implausible in sky130. unrolled_k with k>=4 reduces cycles/result to <=7, making 50 MSPS achievable at realistic Fmax. Therefore, we allocate 90% of the budget to unrolled_k to map its power-accuracy trade-off, and 10% to iterative to confirm its infeasibility and avoid missing any unexpected feasible corner. The parameter ranges for unrolled_k focus on the plausible feasible region: data_width 13-18 (just above the 2^-12 quantization limit), n_iter 10-18 (enough CORDIC iterations with guards), angle_guard -2..3, frac_guard 0..3, both rounding modes, and k 2..8 to cover the parallelism vs. critical-path trade-off. We expect the Pareto front to be dominated by unrolled_k, with power increasing with k, N, W, and guards."
}

